4. PRIOR KINDRED EVENTS — same wedge signature, hypothesis linkage
================================================================================
Member 1 was ejected from the stack 3 times earlier in this session (documented
in 38385.log), ALWAYS with the identical m2-side signature (tipc 6-probe loss ->
"unreachable via Layer-2 traffic" -> ejection), always member 1, and always
4-5 s after a port/config operation touching member-1 ports:
  2026-08-18 23:14:18Z  after "Configuration update completed for
                        port1.0.1-port1.0.28" (tail of its stack join)
  2026-08-18 23:33:49Z  4 s after `no shutdown` on port1.0.9 (+port2.0.9)
  (a third, earlier, around its rejoin during test 38385)
In those events member 1 was the BACKUP: it printed NOTHING on its console
before rebooting — consistent with the same silent wedge, where the i2c line
only prints when the mv64xxx driver's timeout expires and the unit lives long
enough to say so.

HYPOTHESIS (explicitly not proven): one underlying member-1 wedge, two visible
outcomes — as backup it gets TIPC-ejected by the master; as master it wedges
until the watchdog hard-resets it. If so, the field-reported "link flapping on
show tech-support" is the from-outside view of the master wedging/resetting,
not individual PHY flaps. Port/config operations and tech-support collection
would then be two different doors into the same fault. Unit-specificity is
untested: member 2 has never exhibited the wedge, but has also never run
tech-support as master on this bench.

